WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.801
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.802
Thank you very much.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.803
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.538
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.908
[ Cheering and applause ]
Ah!

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.144
Well, guys,
the first week of 2021

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:13.179
was quite a year.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.748
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.517
You know, when I got into comedy
as a teenager,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.119
I never imagined
I would spend three days

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.753
discussing an American coup.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.655
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.524
Honestly, if I knew what
this week was going to be like,

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.359
everyone would've spent
New Year's Eve poppin' bottles

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.427
of Pepto-Bismol.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:28.561
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.062
Yeah, it's been a hell
of a week.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.498
If the country were a rental
car, Trump's returning it

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.166
with an empty tank
and a huge dent.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.069
[ As Trump ]
She's all yours.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.904
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.539
But Trump is
in some serious trouble.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.806
It's sounding like, next week,

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:44.110
he really could be
impeached again.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.879
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, Trump could be

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.881
the first U.S. president
in history

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.717
to get impeached twice.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.885
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.386
And, if Rudy Giuliani
gets involved,

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.787
he could probably
squeeze in a third.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.422
[ Laughter ]
I mean --

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:59.659
[ Applause ]

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.260
No one gets impeached twice.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.996
Do you know how hard
it is to do?

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.164
It's basically O.J.
getting away with it,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.700
then getting nine years
for stealing sports memorabilia.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.002
[ Laughter ]
It can't happen.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.204
It can't.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.405
Seriously,
you know you messed up

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.407
when you're fired
and, on the way out,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.075
you somehow get fired again.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.377
It's like, "Wait. What?"

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.379
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.080
Trump's life is really historic.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.416
He's on track to be the only
president to get elected once,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.416
impeached twice,

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:25.552
and divorced three times.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.353
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.122
Meanwhile, after a 12-hour ban,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.290
Trump's Twitter account
was restored

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.392
and today he tweeted...

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.364
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.532
In related news,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.000
the New York Jets announced
they won't be

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.101
at this year's Super Bowl.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.003
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.139
[ Drumbeat ]

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.774
[ Cymbals crash ]
[ Playing funk ]

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:57.684
♪♪

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.185
[ Laughter ]
-What are you swinging?

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.319
Is that a pocket watch?
-It's a chain.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.688
Yeah, a pocket watch, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.223
-Like the '40s?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:08.928
♪♪

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.263
There you go.
There you go.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.231
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.166
Well, last night,
Trump posted a video on Twitter

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.769
where he tried to bring down
the temperature of the country.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:17.970
Listen to what he said.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.606
-Now, Congress
has certified the results.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:24.310
A new administration will be
inaugurated on January 20th.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.646
My focus now turns to ensuring
a smooth, orderly,

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.716
and seamless transition
of power.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:35.421
This moment calls for healing
and reconciliation.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.856
-Last time I heard someone
that nervous

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:37.857
reading something out loud,

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.891
it was at a bar mitzvah.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.327
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.895
After Trump finished his speech,
he was like --

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.263
[ As Trump ]
Okay, now, can I have dessert?

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.931
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.367
Meanwhile, the riots at the
Capitol are still being examined

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:49.936
and anyone who might've
played a role

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.104
is being investigated.
Listen to this.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.273 line:0%
-Federal prosecutors are saying
they are looking

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.742 line:0%
at all actors involved
in the riot

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:59.111 line:0%
at the Capitol on Wednesday,
including the role

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:02.648 line:0%
that President Trump played
in inciting the crowd.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.817
-If Trump ever goes to prison,
he's going to be really lonely,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.386
since he pardoned all
of his friends.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:10.522
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:13.959
Speaking of,
Trump has suggested to aides

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.862 line:0%
that he wants to pardon himself

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.330 line:0%
in the final days
of his presidency.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.499
Some people are wondering

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.067
if Trump can even pardon
himself, but don't worry.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.503
Rudy Giuliani already
has a bunch

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.505
of soaking wet documents
to prove he can.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.740
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.074
Yeah, a lot of experts
are questioning

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:30.743
if this is legal,
but Trump is like --

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.377
[ As Trump ] In that case,
I'll just pardon myself

00:03:32.377 --> 00:03:33.446
for pardoning myself.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.881
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.682
Meanwhile, in light
of this week's events,

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.818
Trump's Cabinet members
are still stepping down.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.620
Last night,
Education Secretary Betsy DeVos

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.623
submitted her resignation.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.858
Man, even Betsy DeVos is smart
enough to get the hell out.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.961
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.463
Betsy told Trump,
"Mr. President,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.398
it was the best...

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.599
four years in my life."

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.736
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.504
Really wise.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.306
Meanwhile, not all
of Trump's Cabinet members

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.774
have abandoned him
This afternoon,

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.908
Ben Carson was like,

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:04.177
[ Yawning ]
"What'd I miss this week?"

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:07.413
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.581
Say what?

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.550
There's so much going on
in the news right now,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.884
but it seems like not
every network

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.220
is worried about the same thing.
Watch this.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.921 line:0%
-CNN just learned
that Betsy DeVos,

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.558 line:0%
the Education secretary
is resigning.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.293 line:0%
-Head of the Capitol Police
is resigning,

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.694 line:0%
as is the
sergeant of arms of the House

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.095 line:0%
and the sergeant of arms
in the Senate.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.764 line:0%
-Let me just give a plug
for Olive Garden.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.032 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
I like Olive Garden.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.366 line:0%
-The mood inside the
White House,

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.835 line:0%
according to aides,
they say staffers are appalled,

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.205 line:0%
disgusted, and shocked.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:35.007 line:0%
-I like their their salad,
unlimited,

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.276 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
unlimited garlic breadsticks

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:38.477 line:0%
that are phenomenal.

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:40.046 line:0%
-The whole incident raises
a lot of questions

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.980 line:0%
about police preparedness
for the event.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.749 line:0%
-They got these hot,
doughnut-like things

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:46.285 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
that you put like chocolate
sauce with caramel on.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.319 line:0%
Great!

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:49.355
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.957
What?!

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.691
He loves it.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:53.860
Let's switch gears.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.829
I saw that Elon Musk
just passed Jeff Bezos

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.432
as the richest person
in the world.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.934
Anyway, if you can,
hit up Jeff's GoFundMe page

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.669
and let's help him
get back to number 1.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:07.339
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:09.341
Even if you can spare
one billion.

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.210
Any bit helps.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.278
Some sports news.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.745
The NFL playoffs begin
this weekend,

00:05:13.745 --> 00:05:17.115
with 14 teams chasing
at a chance at the Super Bowl.

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:18.384
Seriously,
after this week of news,

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.752
the NFL playoffs are going
to feel like

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.220
watching "Antiques Roadshow."

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.489
[ Laughter ]
And, finally, I saw that a cat

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.159
was recently rescued
after it survived 11 days

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.361
in the ceiling
of LaGuardia Airport.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.528
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:30.729
The cat was like,
"Don't take me.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:32.064
It's all-you-can-eat
rats up here."

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.969
It was quite a scene
at LaGuardia.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.271
Apparently, the cat was rescued,
watched some of the news,

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:40.906
then ran right back
up into the ceiling.

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:44.043
So the other night I was looking
for something to watch

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.244
on, you know.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.578
After the show, I went home

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:50.383
and so Tariq texted me,
"You should check out" --

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.517
I go, "What should I watch?"

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:52.885
He goes, "James told me
about this show,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.321
'Gangs of London.'"
-Yeah.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.790
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. So I put it on.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.525
That's the most violent
show I've ever --

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.759
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.362
-Yeah!
-seen in my entire life.
-It's crazy.

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.664
Yeah.
-You can't watch that
at nighttime.

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:06.966
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, sure you can, man.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.368
-The first 30 seconds,
the dude is throwing a guy

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:11.336
off the side of a building,
then lights him on fire.

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.639
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.375
For good measure.
-Yeah, no, "for good measure."

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.744
No, I can't handle them.

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.313
My brain can't handle that
at nighttime.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.848
-What you do is you watch it,
you watch a couple episodes,

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:24.784
and then you watch like
"Bridgerton" or something,

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.519
like as a little palate cleanser

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:27.853
on your way
before you go to sleep."

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:28.921
[ Laughter ]
-That's what I did.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.990
I, in fact, stopped the episode.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.624
[ Laughter ]
I watched "Bridgerton."

00:06:32.624 --> 00:06:35.327
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. It's like

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:38.531
if "Boardwalk Empire"
and "The Matrix" had a baby.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:42.001
[ Laughter ]
-It's insane!

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.869
-Yeah. It's crazy.
-I made sure the kids were

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:44.871
in the room to watch it.

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.605
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:48.074
"Look at this."

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.675
No, you know what?
What I really did,

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:52.678
I watched "The Office" is
on Peacock.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.046
-Oh, yeah.
-It left Netflix.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.715
It's on Peacock.
And I'm telling you,

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.516
that Peacock thing is good.

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:58.884
-Yeah.
-I like it.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:01.086
It's free. But they did
a good job making that thing.

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.522
But I watched -- I've seen
all the episodes, I think,

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:07.326
but I forget all of them,
so I watched a couple of those.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:09.829
And then I watched --
I saved it for the morning.

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.531
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:12.798
-What episode
-Dude, at one point --

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.634
-did you make it up to?
-Oh, I only finished

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.368
the first episode.
It's a lot for me.
Oh, man,

00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:18.270
it's just getting started.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.139
-Dude, I was crying.
I was afraid.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:22.441
[ Laughter ]
I called 911.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:25.511
[ Laughter ]
At one point, I was going
to call you and go,

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.413
"What's wrong with you?"

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:29.915
I'm not kidding.
He goes into a bar,

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:31.217
takes a dude's leg,

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:33.753
and breaks it sideways
over the bar,

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:35.254
shoves a glass in his mouth

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.656
and takes his head and slams
the dude's head into the bar.

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:38.991
[ Laughter ]
-It's crazy!

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:40.459
-I go, "Okay, kids, get in here!

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:41.527
You're going to love this."

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:45.231
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:47.033
I need my "Office" after that.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.100
I need "Bridgerton."
I need...

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.168
-Something, right?

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:51.003
-Oh, my gosh.
Well, anyways, guys,

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:53.072
we have comedy and fun
for you tonight.

